    "notes": "Saved check 35444, source auction_lot 15710 (Scotch Whisky Auctions 185th auction, lot 185-904492), run 2026-11-03. Production ran without the lot photo: input.reference.imageUrl was null. This case sets it to the lot's first photo at full size and adds that photo's reviewed label reading to the evidence pack; it goes in with the change that makes auctions read the lot photo. The lot's stored sourceImageUrl is the 224px `-med` copy of the same image, too small to read the ABV, so that change needs the `-zoom` (1500px) size. The photo clearly shows the bottle and carton: The Glenturret, Highland Single Malt Scotch Whisky, Triple Wood, 2023 Release, 70cl, 43%vol, and the carton's 'Distilled by The Glenturret Distillery'. The engraving '17 years - Who knew!' on the bottle base is a personal engraving, not an age statement, and is left out of the reading. The lot text and the scraper's structured ABV say 45%, which matches the 2025 Release (46005, 45%), not the 2023 Release. The printed label settles it: 45557 is the same release and no stored field conflicts. 2026-11-04: auction matching now sends the lot photo as imageEvidence (production shape since the photo-reading change), so reference.imageUrl is null and imageEvidence holds a live openai/gpt-6-luna reading of the -zoom photo (43%vol, 2023 Release)."
